
#import "../../../_lib/kodama.typ": *

#show: kodama

#metadata((
  title: "Ramification groups",
))

// Let $(L, lambda, pi.alt)$ and $(K, kappa, pi)$ be local fields and $L slash K$ a finite Galois extension, we write $U_L^((0)) = cal(O)_L^times$ and $U_L^((s)) = 1 + pi.alt^s cal(O)_L$ for $s >= 1$ and $p$ the character of the residue field.

// There exists a surjection of Galois groups $G_(K slash L) -> G_(lambda slash kappa)$ whose kernel is a normal subgroup called the inertia group $I_(K slash L) subset G_(K slash L)$. For every $s >= -1$ we define the $s$-th ramification group which is independent of $pi.alt$:
// $
//   I_(L slash K, s) := {sigma in G_(L slash K) mid(|) sigma(x) - x in pi.alt^(s+1) cal(O)_L, forall x in cal(O)_L}
// $
// Then $I_(L slash K, -1) = G_(L slash K)$ and $I_(L slash K, 0) = I_(L slash K)$. $R_(L slash K) := I_(L slash K, 1)$ is called the ramification group and $I_(L slash K, s)$ are called higher ramification groups. For $s >= 0$, the mapping:
// $
//   I_(L slash K, s)/I_(L slash K, s+1) & -> U_L^((s))/U_L^((s+1)) \
//   sigma & mapsto sigma(pi.alt)/pi.alt
// $
// is injective and independent of $pi.alt$. In particular, $R_(L slash K)$ is the Sylow $p$-subgroup of $I_(L slash K)$.

// Let $g_s = abs(I_(L slash K, s))$. We now define a piecewise linear $phi_(L slash K) : [-1, infinity) -> [-1, infinity)$ by:
// - $phi(0) = 0$
// - The slope on $(s, s+1)$ equals $g_(s+1)/g_0$.
// Or if we define $I_(L slash K, s) = I_(L slash K, ceil(s))$ for $s in RR$, we have:
// $
//   phi(t) = integral_0^t (d s)/([I_(L slash K, 0) : I_(L slash K, s)])
// $
// So that we are able to introduce the upper numbering $I_(L slash K)^(u) := I_(L slash K, phi^(-1)(u))$.

// #subtree(
//   taxon: "proposition"
// )[
//   The upper numbering satisfy for finite Galois extensions $L slash M slash K$ of local fields, we have $I_(M slash K)^(u) = im(I_(L slash K)^u)$.
// ]

// #subtree(
//   title: "Hasse–Arf",
//   taxon: "theorem"
// )[
//   If $L slash K$ is Abelian (possibly infinite), then jumps in $I_(L slash K)^(u)$ are integers.
// ]
